From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] On the variable refresh path, the launch owns synchronization

PortareOS runs every game on the variable refresh path; runemu exports
MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR=1 for it, which Mesa and setsettings read as
well (fixed refresh is left for debugging timing). There frames are
timed at the core's rate with vsync off (0018, 0019) and the display
driver repeats them below the panel's range. Turning vsync on, or Sync
to Exact Content Framerate off, in the menu or with the hotkey, or
through a saved override, left that path for the session or for every
launch.

On that path vsync is off and Sync to Exact Content Framerate on after
the config loads and after an override is loaded or unloaded, both
entries leave the menu (Video > Synchronization, Latency, Frame
Throttle), and the hotkey does nothing. Vsync is not used there at all:
content that does not fit twice into the panel's rate, a few arcade
boards at 60.1 to 63 Hz against 120.198, is refused. drivers_init finds
it from the content's rate; the core never runs, "This game is not
supported" shows for three seconds, and RetroArch quits. With the
variable unset or 0 nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
diff --git a/configuration.c b/configuration.c
--- a/configuration.c
+++ b/configuration.c
@@ -6040,6 +6040,32 @@
 #ifdef HAVE_CONFIGFILE
    config_parse_file(global);
 #endif
+   config_vrr_path_owns_sync(config_st);
+}
+
+/* PortareOS runs every game on the variable refresh path unless black
+ * frame insertion asks for fixed refresh, and runemu says which by
+ * exporting MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR, which Mesa and setsettings read too.
+ * On that path the launch owns synchronization: frames are timed at the
+ * core's rate (Sync to Exact Content Framerate, 0018) with vsync off, and
+ * the display driver repeats them below the panel's range. Neither the
+ * menu, the hotkey nor a saved override turns vsync on there, and content
+ * that does not fit twice into the panel's rate is refused rather than
+ * locked to the display with vsync (runloop_refuse_content). */
+bool config_vrr_path(void)
+{
+   const char *v = getenv("MESA_VK_WSI_DISPLAY_VRR");
+   return v && v[0] == '1' && v[1] == '\0';
+}
+
+void config_vrr_path_owns_sync(settings_t *settings)
+{
+   if (!settings || !config_vrr_path())
+      return;
+   if (settings->bools.video_vsync || !settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
+      RARCH_LOG("[Config] Variable refresh: vsync off, Sync to Exact Content Framerate on.\n");
+   settings->bools.video_vsync        = false;
+   settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable = true;
 }
 
